1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:02,390
Here's the bag.

2
00:00:02,390 --> 00:00:03,800
Will he be OK, Dad?

3
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:09,710
I hope so.

4
00:00:09,710 --> 00:00:11,000
That's it.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,490
That's the way.

6
00:00:12,490 --> 00:00:15,730
That's it. There.

7
00:00:15,730 --> 00:00:18,800
Oh, it's going to be all right.

8
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,070
That's it.

9
00:00:20,070 --> 00:00:22,100
Wrap him in the blanket, Dad!

10
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,010
That's it. That's it.

11
00:00:24,010 --> 00:00:25,940
It's all right, Albert.

12
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:28,630
You're going to be OK.

13
00:00:28,630 --> 00:00:30,030
I want my daddy!

14
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:31,670
We'll take you to him.

15
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:39,140
Easy now. Easy does it. That's it.

16
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:40,940
Your dad is quite a guy.

17
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:42,930
I know, Grandpa.

18
00:00:42,930 --> 00:00:44,590
How is he, Philip?

19
00:00:44,590 --> 00:00:45,700
He's asleep.

20
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:47,170
He's going to be fine.

21
00:00:47,170 --> 00:00:48,550
How can I thank all of you?

22
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:50,020
Thank my son Robbie.

23
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:51,310
He pulled him out of the water.

24
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:52,660
I'm very grateful, Robbie.

25
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:54,530
Dad saved him, not me.

26
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:58,150
I'm so thankful to all of you.

27
00:00:58,150 --> 00:01:00,680
So long.

28
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:02,800
He's a lucky boy.

29
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,640
Well, what do you say we get back to our fishing?

30
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:07,350
That's a great idea.

31
00:01:07,350 --> 00:01:13,070
Uh-oh. It's probably the hospital.

32
00:01:13,070 --> 00:01:15,910
I have to get to a phone.

33
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:18,070
It probably means we can't stay.

34
00:01:18,070 --> 00:01:24,920
That's OK.

35
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:27,080
One of my patients has a high fever,

36
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:29,850
and I have to go to the hospital.

37
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:30,680
I'm sorry, Robbie.

38
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:33,270
I guess I ruined your day.

39
00:01:33,270 --> 00:01:39,920
You didn't ruin my day, Dad.

40
00:01:39,920 --> 00:02:08,500
I understand. I really do.

41
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:10,200
Why are you back so early?

42
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:12,080
Philip had to go back to the hospital.

43
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:13,750
He had an emergency.

44
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:15,780
Oh, that's too bad, Robbie.

45
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:16,970
Did it spoil your fun?

46
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:19,680
No, Mom. We had a great time.

47
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,920
Well, did you do any fishing?

48
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:28,320
Yeah, we caught lots of them. Look!

49
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:31,880
They had a special on frozen fish down at the supermarket.

50
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:35,400
Oh, you really had a bad day.

51
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:37,200
We had a good day.

52
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:40,080
Robbie pulled a boy out of the water.

53
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:42,650
And Dad saved his life.

54
00:02:42,650 --> 00:02:45,300
He's a terrific doctor, Mom.

55
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:58,510
I know.

56
00:02:58,510 --> 00:03:00,560
Hi, Pop. Hi, Son.

57
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,770
Hello, Dad.

58
00:03:02,770 --> 00:03:04,490
What a day!

59
00:03:04,490 --> 00:03:06,470
How about a cup of coffee, Son?

60
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:15,710
I'd love a cup of coffee.

61
00:03:15,710 --> 00:03:17,220
How was the patient?

62
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:19,340
She'll be fine.

63
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:21,610
Was it serious?

64
00:03:21,610 --> 00:03:24,430
No.

65
00:03:24,430 --> 00:03:28,330
Until today, I was never really interested in medicine.

66
00:03:28,330 --> 00:03:30,970
Well, it's hard work.

67
00:03:30,970 --> 00:03:33,450
Now I know.

68
00:03:33,450 --> 00:03:36,690
I had a good time today, Robbie.

69
00:03:36,690 --> 00:03:39,060
Me, too.

70
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:41,100
Why don't we do it again?

71
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:43,710
Can we? When?

72
00:03:43,710 --> 00:03:45,890
How about next Saturday?

73
00:03:45,890 --> 00:03:48,270
Won't you be busy?

74
00:03:48,270 --> 00:03:51,370
I'm changing my schedule.

75
00:03:51,370 --> 00:03:53,250
Well, do we have a date?

76
00:03:53,250 --> 00:03:55,430
We sure do, Dad.

77
00:03:55,430 --> 00:03:57,560
Grandpa, can you come?

78
00:03:57,560 --> 00:04:00,460
I have other plans, Robbie.

79
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:04,630
But I think you two can have a good time together without me.

80
00:04:04,630 --> 00:04:07,630
No, Dad, and certainly not without the right magic.
